{% props class = '' %}
{#
    Single-column page layout — the default shape.

    Renders the page body as one stacked flow inside the wide
    `<main>` element (which shares its width with the header and
    footer at ≈ 1600px, matching the mocks). No extra horizontal
    constraint is applied here — inner components (`<twig:Hero>`,
    `<twig:Box>`, the various form sections, etc.) own whatever
    narrower max-width they need at the section level. Use for
    routes whose body is a single line of content: frontpage,
    login, registration, simple admin forms, error pages.

    The `view-root` class hooks into the global fade-up animation
    in `assets/styles/app.css`, so direct children fade up in
    sequence.

    Slot:
    - `content` — the page body.
#}
<div class="view-root grid grid-cols-1 gap-12{{ class ? ' ' ~ class : '' }}">
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
</div>
